result.Should().BeSuccessful().And.WithValue(expected);
result.Should().BeFailure().And.WithError(expectedError);
```

## Rules

- Return `Result<T>` from every failable method
- Use `Nothing` for void operations
- Never throw for expected domain failures
- Never access `result.Value` without checking `result.IsSuccess` first
- Never return `null`
- Always provide both `Code` and `Description` in `ResultError`
- Prefer LINQ query syntax over nested `OnSuccess` for multi-step pipelines
